                <pb facs="0969" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/296</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Saburi</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acting under instructions from the Japanese
                    Government, I have the honor to inform you that on July 14 the following
                    statement was made public in Tokio: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Japanese Government, considering it expedient to reduce the extent
                            of territory occupied by their troops in the Province of Saghalien, have
                            decided to withdraw by the end of September of this year all of their
                            troops from the districts opposite the Island of Saghalien. As for the
                            northern or Russian part of the Island of Saghalien, it is their
                            intention to terminate occupation as soon as satisfactory settlement for
                            the Nikolaievsk affair has been obtained.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sadao Saburi</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
